# `function one(..) { return first(some(..)); }` with `function first(iter) { if (iter !== undefined) { for (const value of iter) { return value; } } return undefined; }`: a helper that takes the first of whatever
# can be iterated, handed a generator made for it. Outside loops the helper was called. In its own unit nothing is known of its parameter: a guess at a list that never holds, then the iterator is opened, `next` read,
# the step and the close each by a call of the library. TypeScript 6: getUnmatchedProperty(): 0.67 M generators a run.
# A callee without a loop that comes round, no larger than what is copied in loops, that opens an iteration over a parameter is copied where the call hands it what a generator function has just made: what is iterated
# is then a generator of one function: one test that nobody has laid anything above it, and the steps in line.
# f1 = some . f2 = first . f3 = one
# -- source: main.cjs
